# Example for tools/leakscan-local.txt (gitignored, not part of this repo).
#
# tools/check.sh scans the working tree for the patterns listed in
# tools/leakscan-local.txt, if that file exists. It is meant to hold the
# identifiers of *your* installation - database user/name, hostname, admin
# e-mail, SMTP host, and anything else that would help an attacker reach
# your server - so that a `git add` or a copy-pasted config snippet never
# ends up committed.
#
# One extended-regex (grep -E) pattern per line. Lines starting with '#'
# and blank lines are ignored. Copy this file to leakscan-local.txt and
# fill in your own values; that file is gitignored and stays local.
#
# Examples (replace with your real values):
mydbuser123
my-db-host\.example\.com
